Hi Team,


For those of you who have recently signed into CyberArk and noticed the pop-up notification regarding Idira, this phased re-branding transition will begin May 31, 2026.  Please see the below information for additional context on this upcoming change.

 

 

What is Idira?

CyberArk has long been a trusted partner for securing privilege and defending critical assets. Now its becoming Idira - built on CyberArk’s legacy and powered by Palo Alto Networks.

 

Idira is the next-generation identity security platform from Palo Alto Networks, carrying CyberArk’s mission forward and expanding it to match today’s challenges.

 

 

Why is this changing?

CyberArk is now a Palo Alto Networks company, establishing Identity Security as a core pillar of its platformization strategy.  As part of this, the CyberArk brand will begin phased changes to move to Idira, by Palo Alto Networks.

 

 

What is not changing?

With the re-branding, our current access and permissions remain the same.  The Core functionality and workflows will not be impacted as of this initial phase. The Tile we access in Okta will not change immediately, but we will update that to reflect the re-brand and send a notification with a specific tile change date.

 

 

What changes can I expect?

CyberArk is now Idira. Beginning May 31, 2026, we will begin to see some brand changes with their CyberArk products and services, now Idira. These changes will be gradually rolled out in a phased approach, designed to emphasize the new brand and name, while minimizing the impact on customer environments.

 

Phase 1 will begin on May 31, 2026. This phase is focused on visual elements in the product user interface (UI) - updating the logo, illustrations and the previous CyberArk name - as well as updates to product documentation and product-generated automated emails (i.e., status page and platform services).

 

Product-Generated Automated Email Changes:

Email Content: Both the subject lines and body content will reflect the new branding and logo.

Sender Identity: While the sender ID remains unchanged for now, the sender display name may be updated to align with the new brand.

 

Important Note: If you use automations triggered by specific email notifications, please review your configurations, as changes to the display name or subject lines may impact these workflows.

 

 

What is Next?

Following the first phase, they are carefully planning subsequent updates to reflect the new brand across various technical touchpoints, including product URLs, integration tools like APIs, and external system outputs. Recognizing that these deeper technical shifts can have a more direct impact on our environment, they are dedicated to designing these changes with the utmost care to ensure they are as seamless as possible for your operations.

 

This evolution is a journey that won't happen overnight, especially given the long-standing legacy of the CyberArk name. They are committed to a phased, responsible rollout and will provide clear communication well in advance of each new step. By working closely with us, they aim to ensure we are fully prepared and supported as we move into the Idira era together.

 

 

